/** @page ncurses_stylesguide Style System

    @tableofcontents

    @section ncursesstylesfields Colors and Attributes

    Drawing methods accept a @ref Qore::Ncurses::Style "Style" hash:
    - \c fg: foreground color from @ref Qore::Ncurses::Color "Color".
    - \c bg: background color from @ref Qore::Ncurses::Color "Color".
    - \c attrs: bitwise OR of @ref Qore::Ncurses::Attr "Attr" values, such as bold and underline.

    Omit unused fields. @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::supportsColor() "Session::supportsColor()"
    reports whether colors are active. @ref Qore::Ncurses::Color "Color::Default" selects the
    terminal default when the session enables default colors. The available palette depends
    on the terminal; inspect @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::maxColors() "Session::maxColors()"
    before using additional color indexes.

    @section ncursesstylesexample Borders and Styled Lines

    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::box() "Window::box()" draws a border. The
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::drawTextInsideLine() "Window::drawTextInsideLine()" helper uses
    coordinates inside that border and clears the unused part of the line, so shorter updates
    do not leave old characters behind. Run this example in a terminal at least 5 rows high:

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses

Ncurses::Session session();
on_exit session.close();
Ncurses::Window window = session.screen();
hash<Ncurses::Style> heading = <Ncurses::Style>{
    "fg": Ncurses::Color::Yellow,
    "bg": Ncurses::Color::Blue,
    "attrs": Ncurses::Attr::Bold | Ncurses::Attr::Underline,
};
window.clear();
window.box({"fg": Ncurses::Color::Cyan});
window.drawTextInsideLine(0, "Service status", heading);
window.drawTextInsideLine(1, "Ready", {"fg": Ncurses::Color::Green});
window.drawTextInsideLine(2, "Press a key to close");
window.refresh();
window.readEvent();
    @endcode

    @section ncursesstyleswrapping Clipping and Wrapping

    Use @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::drawTextClipped() "Window::drawTextClipped()" for text that
    may exceed the surface, and @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::drawTextInside() "Window::drawTextInside()"
    to preserve a border. Set multiline wrapping with
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::setWrapMode() "Window::setWrapMode()" and
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::WrapMode "WrapMode" (none, hard wrap, or word wrap).
    See @ref ncurses_ansiguide "ANSI SGR Text" for colors embedded in strings and
    @ref NcursesUi::TerminalText "TerminalText" for Unicode-aware plain-text alignment.
*/
